<SubSection title="Convective Heat Transfer Coefficient" id="HeatTransferCoeff"> 
<p>Solving for the Heat Transfer Coefficient (h):</p>
<Itemize>
<Item> Identify the solid's geometry: flat plate, cylinder, or sphere.</Item>
<Item> Find L (Characteristic Length)</Item>
<Item> Identify natural or forced convection</Item>
<Item> Identify if the flow is laminar or turbulent using the Reynold's Number</Item>
<Item> Choose the equation!</Item>
</Itemize>

<CalloutContainer slot="cards">
    <CalloutCard title="Heads Up!">
     <p> When considering convection over a surface, the characteristic length (L) refers to how far the fluid must travel over/around the system. This differs from the characteristic length (L) used in the Conduction section, where L was the path of least resistance for heat to leave an object. </p>
    </CalloutCard>
</CalloutContainer>


